==English==

===Etymology===
From a 1990 article by Morning Glory Zell-Ravenheart, "A Bouquet of Lovers", from {{af|en|poly-|amorous}} or {{af|en|polyamory|-ous}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Having [[relationship]]s with multiple [[partner]]s, with the knowledge and consent of all involved; engaging in [[polyamory]].
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Zachary Zane|title=Where Do "Messy Bisexuals" Fit Into the Bi+ Community?|work=w:HuffPost|url=https://www.huffpost.com/entry/where-do-messy-bisexuals_b_9558876|date=3 April 2016|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20220607120850/https://www.huffpost.com/entry/heres-why-a-genderqueer-polyromantic-demisexual_b_57ec2588e4b07f20daa101a2|archivedate=7 June 2022|passage=Being '''polyamorous''' isn't inherently wrong. Neither is desiring threesomes or kinky sex.}}
# Open to having such relationships, regardless of one's experience or current practices.

